  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Show that $8^n-5^n$ is divisible by $3$ for every natural number $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8^n-5^n\\equiv0\\pmod3$.\n\nBoth bases are congruent to $2$ modulo $3$, so their powers have the same remainder.",
      "worked": "Since $8\\equiv2\\pmod3$ and $5\\equiv2\\pmod3$, the exponentiation and subtraction rules give\n$$\\begin{align*}8^n-5^n&\\equiv2^n-2^n\\pmod3,\\\\8^n-5^n&\\equiv0\\pmod3.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $8^n-5^n$ is divisible by $3$ for every natural number $n$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
